From 98fe4c7e89b5295a5f11fcc639daf7b6dbf51156 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:56:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kpi: managed device pagers (pager.rs)

OBJT_MGTDEVICE objects for d_mmap_single whose pages the driver can take
back from every mapping. The handle is a Box<T> owned by the object and
freed by the pager destructor; T only chooses the physical address for a
fault, and the fault path refuses anything that is not an unowned
fictitious page, so a wrong answer cannot map RAM or steal a page.
VmObject<T> is one object reference (Clone takes another, Drop gives it
back). bindings.h: the vm_object/vm_page/vm_pager headers, and the
object lock and page xunbusy macros as functions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
